    "description": "Ksar Aït Benhaddou, Marocco Aït Benhaddou (Arabic: آيت بن حدّو) is a historic ighrem or ksar (fortified village) along the former caravan route between the Sahara and Marrakesh in Morocco. It is considered a great example of Moroccan earthen clay architecture and has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1987. World Heritage Site Moroccan cultural heritage: ID Q309436"
  },
